  "estudio": "Hei!",
  "alumno": "Greeting and introducing yourself"
 },
 "intro": "In written Bokmål, **hei** is used to greet both people you know and people you have just met. In Norwegian, **du** is used even with strangers, so there is no everyday split between a polite and a familiar «you», much as in English, which has only one «you». **De** exists, but today it usually sounds very formal or old-fashioned. The pronunciations are approximations of eastern Norwegian speech; there is dialect variation.",
