  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Greeting and saying your name",
     "texto": [
      "Hei! is the most common greeting. Hallo! is also used, for example, when answering the phone. God dag is a slightly more formal greeting.",
      "Ha det! is used to say goodbye. Takk means «thanks», and ja / nei mean «yes / no».",
      "To introduce yourself: Jeg heter Anna («My name is Anna»). To ask: Hva heter du? («What is your name?»). Unlike English «I am» and «you are», heter does not change between jeg and du."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "A friendly phrase",
     "texto": [
      "Hyggelig å hilse på deg is equivalent to «Nice to meet you». Hyggelig literally means «pleasant», but in this greeting it is not translated word for word. Å marks the infinitive, like «to» in «to greet»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
